10.3 Exercise 3
Titanic passengers with a shared ticket can be considered a ticket group. Typically, a ticket group comprised family members, friends, or domestic workers employed by the family.
Question: How many ticket groups lost at least one member at sea?

How many ticket groups lost at least one member at sea?

Hint: check group_by() info here.

ticket_groups &lt;- people |&gt;
  group_by(ticket) |&gt;
  summarize(any_died = any(!survived), .groups = "drop")

ticket_groups |&gt;
  filter(any_died == TRUE) |&gt;
  summarize(n = n())

# A tibble: 1 × 1
      n
  &lt;int&gt;
1   669

11.2 BTC Monthly Prices

btc_monthly &lt;- tq_get(
  "BTC-USD",
  from = "2020-01-01",
  to = Sys.Date(),
  get = "stock.prices"
) |&gt;
  select(date, adjusted) |&gt;
  mutate(date = floor_date(date, "month")) |&gt;
  group_by(date) |&gt;
  summarise(adjusted = last(adjusted), .groups = "drop")

model_btc &lt;- auto.arima(btc_monthly$adjusted)

model_btc |&gt;
  forecast(h = 24) |&gt;
  autoplot() +
  labs(
    x = "Sample Index",
    y = "Price",
    title = "ARIMA Forecast of BTC Monthly Adjusted Close Prices"
  ) +
  set_theme()
